From: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:10:32 -0700
Subject: gpu: Check GL errors before marking passthrough shared image cleared

The passthrough decoder lazily clears uncleared shared images when a
texture is created for them. Flush pending GL errors into the decoder's
error state before the clear, and only mark the image cleared if no
errors were raised and the context was not lost.

Bug: 566384898
Change-Id: I65f691941291e6ca6de54599bbc337ef5fa4c289
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8526899
Commit-Queue: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1719864}

